system trust store for Kubernetes API | dashboard-operator/config/webhook/manifests.yaml:51 |\n491\t| **Non-FIPS crypto risks** | None detected in Go components; protobuf duplicate-registration conflict between mlflow-go and OTel SDK suppressed at warning level via GOLANG_PROTOBUF_REGISTRATION_CONFLICT=warn | Dockerfile.konflux.genai:99-103 |\n492\t\n493\tAll Go binaries (dashboard-operator and all BFF sidecars) are built with `CGO_ENABLED=1` and `-tags strictfipsruntime`, ensuring dynamic linking to system OpenSSL for FIPS-validated cryptographic operations. The Node.js backend inherits FIPS-capable OpenSSL from its UBI9/nodejs-22 base image but does not have an explicit FIPS opt-in at the application level. No `GOEXPERIMENT=strictfipsruntime` flag is used; FIPS enforcement relies on the `-tags` build constraint. [source: Dockerfile.konflux.dashboard-operator:18-20, Dockerfile.konflux.genai:86, Dockerfile.konflux:34]\n494\t## Admission Webhooks\n495\t\n496\t| Name | Type | Path | Port | Failure Policy | Resources | Operations | Purpose |\n497\t|----|----|----|----|--------------|---------|----------|-------|\n498\t| validate.dashboards.components.platform.opendatahub.io | Validating | /validate-dashboard |  | Fail | dashboards | CREATE |  |\n499\t| vworkspace.kb.io | validating | /validate-kubeflow-org-v1beta1-workspace |  | fail | workspaces | CREATE, UPDATE |  |\n500\t| vworkspacekind.kb.io | validating | /validate-kubeflow-org-v1beta1-workspacekind |  | fail | workspacekinds | CREATE, DELETE, UPDATE |  |\n501\t| workspacekinds.kubeflow.org | conversion | /convert |  |  | workspacekinds | CONVERT |  |\n502\t\n503\t## Data Flows\n504\t\n505\t- **User request path:** Browser clients connect to the dashboard through an OpenShift Route that terminates TLS and forwards traffic to kube-rbac-proxy (port 8443). Kube-rbac-proxy validates the user's OpenShift OAuth token and injects identity headers (`x-forwarded-access-token`, `x-auth-request-user`, `x-auth-request-groups`) before forwarding to the Node.js Fastify backend. The backend serves the React SPA for UI requests at `/` and proxies `/api/k8s/*` requests to the Kubernetes API using user token impersonation. Module federation remotes are served at `/_mf/:name/*` paths, loading domain-specific UI bundles dynamically. [source: backend/src/utils/constants.ts:18-20, backend/src/utils/proxy.ts:39-42, backend/src/routes/root.ts:1, backend/src/routes/module-federation.ts:1]\n506\t- **BFF sidecar traffic:** Each federated module's API calls are routed by path prefix to the corresponding Go BFF sidecar (e.g., `/gen-ai/api/*` → port 8143, `/model-registry/api/*` → port 8043, `/agent-ops/api/*` → port 8843). BFF sidecars authenticate requests independently using Bearer tokens, perform SubjectAccessReviews for authorization, and issue Kubernetes API calls using either the user's forwarded token or an internal ServiceAccount token, depending on the configured `auth-method` flag. Two Kubernetes Service objects expose the operator's metrics (port 8443) and webhook (port 443→9443) endpoints internally. [source: manifests/rhoai/base/federation-configmap.yaml:15, packages/gen-ai/bff/internal/constants/api_constants.go:15, dashboard-operator/config/webhook/manifests.yaml:29]\n507\t- **Controller reconciliation:** The dashboard-operator watches the Dashboard CR (created by rhods-operator) and reconciles the deployment of the console pod, RBAC resources, routes, and services. It also watches platform CRDs (DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization, KServe InferenceService, ModelRegistry, MLflow, TrustyAI, Feast) to propagate platform state changes into dashboard configuration. The Workspace controller reconciles Workspace and WorkspaceKind CRs, managing StatefulSets, Services, and PodDisruptionBudgets for notebook workspaces. [source: dashboard-operator/charts/dashboard/values.yaml:15-18, dashboard-operator/config/rbac/role.yaml:1]\n508\t- **External service interactions:** BFF sidecars proxy requests to external platform services: gen-ai BFF connects to Llama Stack servers, MLflow tracking servers, NeMo guardrails, and MCP servers (via SSE/streamable HTTP with `X-MCP-Bearer` authentication); eval-hub BFF queries TrustyAI and KServe InferenceServices; maas BFF communicates with MaaS API servers; and the core-bff proxies to Prometheus/Thanos for metrics dashboards. All external connections use TLS encryption with Bearer token or API key authentication. [source: packages/gen-ai/bff/internal/constants/mcp.go:5-16, packages/eval-hub/bff/internal/api/inferenceservices_handler.go:94]\n509\t\n510\t## Integration Points\n511\t\n512\t- **/v1/ConfigMap:** Controller watch (Owns); protocol: Kubernetes API; purpose: Controller reconciliation. [source: backend/package.json:2, 54, backend/src/plugins/kube.ts:16, backend/src/routes/api/service/mlmd/index.ts:1, backend/src/routes/api/service/model-serving/index.ts:34]\n513\t- **/v1/ConfigMap:** Resource CRUD; purpose: create, delete, get, list, update operations by App, ClusterSettingsRepository, ConnectionTypeRepository, DashboardReconciler, ModelRegistrySettingsRepository, SharedClientLogic, TokenKubernetesClient, TokenKubernetesClientMock, WorkspaceKindReconciler, WorkspaceKindRepository. [source: backend/package.json:2, 54, backend/src/plugins/kube.ts:16, backend/src/routes/api/service/mlmd/index.ts:1, backend/src/routes/api/service/model-serving/index.ts:34]\n514\t- **/v1/Event:** Resource read; purpose: list operations by WorkspaceReconciler. [source: backend/package.json:2, 54, backend/src/plugins/kube.ts:16, backend/src/routes/api/service/mlmd/index.ts:1, backend/src/routes/api/service/model-serving/index.ts:34]\n515\t- **/v1/Namespace:** Resource CRUD; purpose: create, get, list operations by NamespaceRepository, TokenKubernetesClient, TokenKubernetesClientMock. [source: backend/package.json:2, 54, backend/src/plugins/kube.ts:16, backend/src/routes/api/service/mlmd/index.ts:1, backend/src/routes/api/service/model-servi