{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-d630013b-43ef-4eea-a1b3-99bd251cbf96","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e2fc98e0f9cabfb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-7pc41hkd/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-E002.md","content":"# Configure the remote pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio playground\n\n## Description\n\nMakes Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows use a remote, pgvector-backed vector store through\nthe OGX vector_io provider configuration, so they no longer depend on the inline Milvus provider\nthat is being removed from the OGX distribution (RHAISTRAT-7474). The existing remote vector store\nimplementation in OGX is reusable for pgvector; the change here is configuration: the gen-ai BFF\nin odh-dashboard, which creates and configures OGXServer instances for the playground, sets the\npgvector vector_io provider and consumes the PostgreSQL connection for it.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Gen-ai BFF changes (odh-dashboard, playground OGXServer provisioning code) to configure the\n  remote pgvector vector_io provider (the `remote::pgvector` provider guarded by `ENABLE_PGVECTOR`)\n  on OGXServer instances created for playgrounds with RAG enabled.\n- Consume the PostgreSQL connection details from a reference/secret rather than hardcoding them,\n  so the same configuration path works whether the database is self-provisioned by the platform,\n  provided by the user, or — later — the shared platform-provided database (RHOAI 3.6). This is\n  also the migration path to production-grade vector databases.\n- Keep the OGX application storage backend untouched (existing SQLite defaults) — vector storage\n  and application storage are independent configurations; no storage consolidation and no\n  SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration is in scope.\n- Provide a reversible configuration path (feature flag or equivalent toggle) so the prior\n  behavior can be restored while inline providers still ship in the distribution.\n- Ensure the PostgreSQL image reference used by the configuration flow resolves through the\n  platform's related-image environment variable so disconnected installations work.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A playground with RAG enabled gets an OGXServer instance whose vector_io provider is the remote\n  pgvector provider, running as a separate process decoupled from the OGX instance (not inline).\n- Playground RAG workflows (document upload, embedding, retrieval-augmented chat) function against\n  the pgvector-backed vector store with no loss of current capability, measured against the\n  current playground RAG behavior.\n- The application storage backend of the OGX instance is unchanged from its existing default.\n- The pgvector configuration is reversible: a configuration toggle restores the prior inline\n  behavior while inline providers remain in the distribution.\n- Connection details are consumed via a reference/secret — the same code path works for a\n  self-provisioned, user-provided, or platform-shared PostgreSQL connection string.\n- The PostgreSQL image reference resolves via the platform related-image variable in disconnected\n  installation scenarios.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box): provider-configuration half; the\n  provisioning half is delivered by the selected provisioning approach.\n- AC-2 (playground RAG workflows function with no loss of capability): primary coverage.\n- AC-4 (vector store runs as a separate process, not an inline provider): remote provider by\n  design.\n- Addresses the strategy's open question on migration path: the connection-reference design is\n  the migration path to production-grade vector databases.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Depends on a PostgreSQL instance being reachable via the connection reference; which side\n  provisions it is decided by the go/no-go gate and delivered by the corresponding provisioning\n  work — this epic's code is path-independent by design.\n- If the OGXServer CR surface does not currently expose the fields needed for the pgvector\n  provider configuration, extending that surface is in-epic work (the ogx-k8s-operator already\n  renders runtime configuration into ConfigMaps for OGXServer instances).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":86052,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e4171350d16bb3c","agent_id":"a769685b3c6544b0d","session_id":"eb96f7e6-35e1-46c5-82db-a48f5def6ca9","uuid":"05e5894f-91be-4187-b5d4-406fb0ae1184","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:26:54.951Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
