and adjusted based on the\n  benchmark, suitable for resource-constrained environments.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A benchmark report exists that records the inline Milvus baseline and the pgvector measurements\n  for representative playground RAG workloads, with methodology documented.\n- The report states whether pgvector is in the same order of magnitude as the inline Milvus\n  baseline, with the underlying measurements.\n- A resource-sizing recommendation (requests/limits) is documented, referencing the\n  model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL values as the starting point, and is handed to the\n  provisioning work.\n- No latency SLA thresholds are introduced (dev-experimentation scope is stated in the report).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- AC-2 (playground RAG workflows function with no loss of current capability): verification half —\n  the benchmark is the measured comparison against current capability.\n- AC-6 (default vector store lightweight enough for resource-constrained environments): the\n  sizing recommendation and order-of-magnitude check are the evidence.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The inline Milvus baseline must be captured before RHAISTRAT-7474 removes inline providers from\n  the distribution — a timing constraint on the baseline half of this work.\n- Tier-1 work by design: this epic does not wait for the provisioning go/no-go decision; it may\n  benchmark against a manually provisioned pgvector instance.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":86052,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e4171350d16bb3c","agent_id":"a769685b3c6544b0d","session_id":"eb96f7e6-35e1-46c5-82db-a48f5def6ca9","uuid":"5e72194e-813a-400b-8806-4b8c1e4d6388","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:27:03.921Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
