{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-7ed67bed-ec0a-45ca-af14-b6a828a962e3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9076b956e734aeda","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-7pc41hkd/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E003.md","content":"# Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector self-provisioning for Gen AI Studio (branch A)\n\n## Description\n\nBranch A of the provisioning go/no-go gate — executed if the RHOAI-controlled operator layer\n(the dashboard operator modularization, RHAISTRAT-7164) is available in time for the target\nrelease. Implements Gen AI Studio's PostgreSQL/pgvector lifecycle management in that operator,\nfollowing the model-registry-operator's pattern of auto-provisioning a PostgreSQL database per\nmanaged instance: each namespace with a RAG-enabled playground gets its own pgvector-capable\nPostgreSQL, with the connection surfaced for the playground's OGX vector_io provider\nconfiguration to consume. No custom image build and no Konflux onboarding are needed: the\nexisting Red Hat PostgreSQL image already includes pgvector, and the related-image variable for\nit is already present in the platform operator's CSV for disconnected installs.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Reconciliation logic in the RHOAI-controlled Gen AI Studio operator layer (delivered by\n  RHAISTRAT-7164) that provisions a per-namespace PostgreSQL instance with pgvector for\n  RAG-enabled playgrounds, using the existing Red Hat postgresql-16 image (no custom image,\n  no new pipeline onboarding).\n- Credentials managed via a Secret; connection details surfaced as a consumable reference for the\n  playground OGX vector_io provider configuration.\n- Resource requests/limits starting from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL values,\n  adjustable from the sprint-1 benchmark results.\n- Image reference resolved through the existing related-image environment variable for\n  disconnected installations.\n- Lifecycle management: per-namespace scoping for multi-tenant isolation, and cleanup when the\n  owning playground is deleted.\n- Portability: the consuming configuration must be able to switch to the shared platform-provided\n  PostgreSQL connection string (RHOAI 3.6) without rework.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A RAG-enabled playground in a namespace gets a per-namespace pgvector-capable PostgreSQL\n  instance with no manual user provisioning or configuration of external infrastructure.\n- The provisioned database runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance (not an\n  inline provider).\n- No custom container image is built: the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image (pgvector included)\n  is used, referenced via the platform related-image variable so disconnected installs work.\n- Resource requests/limits follow the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL values as the starting\n  point, with any adjustment from the sprint-1 benchmark documented.\n- Deleting the owning playground cleans up the provisioned PostgreSQL resources.\n- The connection is exposed to the playground configuration as a reference that can later be\n  swapped for the shared platform database connection string without rework.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box): provisioning half of the requirement.\n- AC-4 (runs as a separate process, not inline).\n- AC-5 (scoped for multi-tenant environments, per-namespace isolation).\n- AC-6 (lightweight enough for resource-constrained environments): resource sizing scope.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- This branch exists only if the go/no-go gate selects the operator path; if the operator layer\n  does not land in time, the BFF-managed provisioning path (or bring-your-own PostgreSQL) delivers\n  the default vector store instead.\n- The operator layer's actual API surface is not known until RHAISTRAT-7164 delivers; the\n  reconciliation design adapts to that surface.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":87794,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e4171350d16bb3c","agent_id":"a769685b3c6544b0d","session_id":"eb96f7e6-35e1-46c5-82db-a48f5def6ca9","uuid":"43bcfd64-4f21-43fe-b9ae-b48bb04b1b61","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:27:17.476Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
