{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9273496ee9890c4e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n3\ttitle: Provisioning approach go/no-go gate for the default vector store\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: dashboard-crimson-scrum\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Provisioning approach go/no-go gate for the default vector store\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves the strategy's central uncertainty before the provisioning work is committed: whether the\n30\tRHOAI-controlled operator layer (the dashboard operator modularization tracked as RHAISTRAT-7164,\n31\tIn Progress) will be available in time for the target release, and therefore which provisioning\n32\tapproach the Gen AI Studio default vector store uses — operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector\n33\tself-provisioning following the model-registry-operator pattern (primary path), or gen-ai\n34\tBFF-managed provisioning (fallback path), with bring-your-own PostgreSQL as the last-resort\n35\tfallback. The Staff Engineer Input directs the development team to define this go/no-go gate as\n36\tpart of sprint planning; this epic makes that decision a first-class deliverable.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Define the go/no-go criteria and the decision date for the RHAISTRAT-7164 dependency (what\n41\t  \"lands in time\" means for the target release commitment).\n42\t- Track RHAISTRAT-7164 delivery status against those criteria.\n43\t- Evaluate the fallback path's known caveats so the decision is informed rather than defaulted:\n44\t  cleanup on playground deletion, handling of pod restarts, and credential rotation in a\n45\t  BFF that is not an operator with a reconciliation loop.\n46\t- Confirm the portability requirement that applies to whichever path is chosen: the consuming\n47\t  configuration must be able to switch to the shared platform-provided PostgreSQL connection\n48\t  string when it becomes available (RHOAI 3.6) without rework.\n49\t- Record the decision (chosen approach, rationale, criteria, date) and communicate it to the\n50\t  Gen AI Studio lead and engineering team.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- A written decision exists that states the go/no-go criteria, the decision date, the tracked\n55\t  status of RHAISTRAT-7164 against those criteria, and the selected provisioning approach.\n56\t- The decision is unambiguous: a downstream implementer can tell, from the decision alone, whether\n57\t  operator-based self-provisioning or BFF-managed provisioning is being built (or that the\n58\t  bring-your-own-PostgreSQL fallback is being taken, and why).\n59\t- The fallback-path caveats (lifecycle management without a reconciliation loop) are evaluated\n60\t  and the evaluation is referenced by the decision.\n61\t- The decision is reviewed with the Gen AI Studio lead and the engineering team (sprint planning).\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\t- Enables AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box): determines which provisioning\n66\t  epic exists and what it does.\n67\t- Informs AC-5 (multi-tenant scoping): confirms per-namespace scoping for Gen AI Studio.\n68\t- Governs the strategy's success criterion that RHAISTRAT-7474 (inline provider removal) is\n69\t  unblocked by a viable platform-level replacement.\n70\t\n71\t## Risks / Notes\n72\t\n73\t- The gating input (RHAISTRAT-7164 delivery timing) is externally controlled; this epic's\n74\t  deliverable is the decision and its criteria, not the dependency's delivery. Schedule risk from\n75\t  dependency slippage belongs here as a note, not as an acceptance criterion.\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac7f19a9efafe13c","agent_id":"a7ed42b29d881bc12","session_id":"eb96f7e6-35e1-46c5-82db-a48f5def6ca9","uuid":"a1125523-41f8-4a7d-b544-93856be2150c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:29:54.572Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9273496ee9890c4e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
