{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0a3a1f0e7e47ebc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n3\ttitle: Configure the remote pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio playground\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: dashboard-crimson-scrum\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Configure the remote pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio playground\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tMakes Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows use a remote, pgvector-backed vector store through\n34\tthe OGX vector_io provider configuration, so they no longer depend on the inline Milvus provider\n35\tthat is being removed from the OGX distribution (RHAISTRAT-7474). The existing remote vector store\n36\timplementation in OGX is reusable for pgvector; the change here is configuration: the gen-ai BFF\n37\tin odh-dashboard, which creates and configures OGXServer instances for the playground, sets the\n38\tpgvector vector_io provider and consumes the PostgreSQL connection for it.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Gen-ai BFF changes (odh-dashboard, playground OGXServer provisioning code) to configure the\n43\t  remote pgvector vector_io provider (the `remote::pgvector` provider guarded by `ENABLE_PGVECTOR`)\n44\t  on OGXServer instances created for playgrounds with RAG enabled.\n45\t- Consume the PostgreSQL connection details from a reference/secret rather than hardcoding them,\n46\t  so the same configuration path works whether the database is self-provisioned by the platform,\n47\t  provided by the user, or — later — the shared platform-provided database (RHOAI 3.6). This is\n48\t  also the migration path to production-grade vector databases.\n49\t- Keep the OGX application storage backend untouched (existing SQLite defaults) — vector storage\n50\t  and application storage are independent configurations; no storage consolidation and no\n51\t  SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration is in scope.\n52\t- Provide a reversible configuration path (feature flag or equivalent toggle) so the prior\n53\t  behavior can be restored while inline providers still ship in the distribution.\n54\t- Ensure the PostgreSQL image reference used by the configuration flow resolves through the\n55\t  platform's related-image environment variable so disconnected installations work.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- A playground with RAG enabled gets an OGXServer instance whose vector_io provider is the remote\n60\t  pgvector provider, running as a separate process decoupled from the OGX instance (not inline).\n61\t- Playground RAG workflows (document upload, embedding, retrieval-augmented chat) function against\n62\t  the pgvector-backed vector store with no loss of current capability, measured against the\n63\t  current playground RAG behavior.\n64\t- The application storage backend of the OGX instance is unchanged from its existing default.\n65\t- The pgvector configuration is reversible: a configuration toggle restores the prior inline\n66\t  behavior while inline providers remain in the distribution.\n67\t- Connection details are consumed via a reference/secret — the same code path works for a\n68\t  self-provisioned, user-provided, or platform-shared PostgreSQL connection string.\n69\t- The PostgreSQL image reference resolves via the platform related-image variable in disconnected\n70\t  installation scenarios.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box): provider-configuration half; the\n75\t  provisioning half is delivered by the selected provisioning approach.\n76\t- AC-2 (playground RAG workflows function with no loss of capability): primary coverage.\n77\t- AC-4 (vector store runs as a separate process, not an inline provider): remote provider by\n78\t  design.\n79\t- Addresses the strategy's open question on migration path: the connection-reference design is\n80\t  the migration path to production-grade vector databases.\n81\t\n82\t## Risks / Notes\n83\t\n84\t- Depends on a PostgreSQL instance being reachable via the connection reference; which side\n85\t  provisions it is decided by the go/no-go gate and delivered by the corresponding provisioning\n86\t  work — this epic's code is path-independent by design.\n87\t- If the OGXServer CR surface does not currently expose the fields needed for the pgvector\n88\t  provider configuration, extending that surface is in-epic work (the ogx-k8s-operator already\n89\t  renders runtime configuration into ConfigMaps for OGXServer instances).\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac7f19a9efafe13c","agent_id":"a7ed42b29d881bc12","session_id":"eb96f7e6-35e1-46c5-82db-a48f5def6ca9","uuid":"899f3e96-361f-4879-a1d5-db6c236341d0","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:29:55.239Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0a3a1f0e7e47ebc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
