{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9585dc862d720a9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E003\n3\ttitle: Benchmark pgvector against the inline Milvus baseline and set PostgreSQL resource\n4\t  sizing\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: dashboard-crimson-scrum\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 0\n17\t  open_questions: 1\n18\t  external_dependency: 0\n19\t  human_process_gates: 0\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 4\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Benchmark pgvector against the inline Milvus baseline and set PostgreSQL resource sizing\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tSprint-1 validation work that de-risks the pgvector default before and while the provisioning\n36\tapproach is decided: capture the inline Milvus provider's performance baseline (before inline\n37\tproviders are removed from the distribution), verify that pgvector performs in the same order of\n38\tmagnitude for typical playground RAG usage, and establish the PostgreSQL resource\n39\trequests/limits for the default instance. Per the Staff Engineer Input, the default pgvector\n40\tinstance is for development experimentation: no strict latency SLAs (p50/p95/p99) are required,\n41\ttypical playground RAG usage involves small document sets for which a flat scan (no index) is\n42\tsufficient, and users with production-scale vector workloads are directed to an external vector\n43\tdatabase.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- A repeatable benchmark that exercises representative playground RAG workloads (small document\n48\t  sets: document upload, embedding, retrieval) against a vector store.\n49\t- Baseline capture on the current inline Milvus provider while it still ships in the distribution.\n50\t- Equivalent measurements against a pgvector-backed vector store (a manually provisioned pgvector\n51\t  instance is acceptable for sprint-1 timing if the selected provisioning approach is not yet\n52\t  delivered).\n53\t- An order-of-magnitude comparison report — explicitly not a pass/fail latency-threshold exercise.\n54\t- A PostgreSQL resource-sizing recommendation (requests/limits) for the default instance, starting\n55\t  from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL resource values and adjusted based on the\n56\t  benchmark, suitable for resource-constrained environments.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- A benchmark report exists that records the inline Milvus baseline and the pgvector measurements\n61\t  for representative playground RAG workloads, with methodology documented.\n62\t- The report states whether pgvector is in the same order of magnitude as the inline Milvus\n63\t  baseline, with the underlying measurements.\n64\t- A resource-sizing recommendation (requests/limits) is documented, referencing the\n65\t  model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL values as the starting point, and is handed to the\n66\t  provisioning work.\n67\t- No latency SLA thresholds are introduced (dev-experimentation scope is stated in the report).\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- AC-2 (playground RAG workflows function with no loss of current capability): verification half —\n72\t  the benchmark is the measured comparison against current capability.\n73\t- AC-6 (default vector store lightweight enough for resource-constrained environments): the\n74\t  sizing recommendation and order-of-magnitude check are the evidence.\n75\t\n76\t## Risks / Notes\n77\t\n78\t- The inline Milvus baseline must be captured before RHAISTRAT-7474 removes inline providers from\n79\t  the distribution — a timing constraint on the baseline half of this work.\n80\t- Tier-1 work by design: this epic does not wait for the provisioning go/no-go decision; it may\n81\t  benchmark against a manually provisioned pgvector instance.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac7f19a9efafe13c","agent_id":"a7ed42b29d881bc12","session_id":"eb96f7e6-35e1-46c5-82db-a48f5def6ca9","uuid":"0097a820-0cd5-4bb6-b5d2-6d1df97379a2","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:29:55.947Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9585dc862d720a9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
