{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92a742eee52cd0e2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E003\n3\ttitle: Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector self-provisioning for Gen AI Studio\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: dashboard-crimson-scrum\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the operator layer does not land in time (gate outcome is\n16\t    not A), this epic does not run; the BFF-managed provisioning path delivers the\n17\t    default vector store instead, with bring-your-own PostgreSQL as the further fallback.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 0\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: -1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 3\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector self-provisioning for Gen AI Studio (branch A)\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tBranch A of the provisioning go/no-go gate — executed if the RHOAI-controlled operator layer\n39\t(the dashboard operator modularization, RHAISTRAT-7164) is available in time for the target\n40\trelease. Implements Gen AI Studio's PostgreSQL/pgvector lifecycle management in that operator,\n41\tfollowing the model-registry-operator's pattern of auto-provisioning a PostgreSQL database per\n42\tmanaged instance: each namespace with a RAG-enabled playground gets its own pgvector-capable\n43\tPostgreSQL, with the connection surfaced for the playground's OGX vector_io provider\n44\tconfiguration to consume. No custom image build and no Konflux onboarding are needed: the\n45\texisting Red Hat PostgreSQL image already includes pgvector, and the related-image variable for\n46\tit is already present in the platform operator's CSV for disconnected installs.\n47\t\n48\t## Scope\n49\t\n50\t- Reconciliation logic in the RHOAI-controlled Gen AI Studio operator layer (delivered by\n51\t  RHAISTRAT-7164) that provisions a per-namespace PostgreSQL instance with pgvector for\n52\t  RAG-enabled playgrounds, using the existing Red Hat postgresql-16 image (no custom image,\n53\t  no new pipeline onboarding).\n54\t- Credentials managed via a Secret; connection details surfaced as a consumable reference for the\n55\t  playground OGX vector_io provider configuration.\n56\t- Resource requests/limits starting from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL values,\n57\t  adjustable from the sprint-1 benchmark results.\n58\t- Image reference resolved through the existing related-image environment variable for\n59\t  disconnected installations.\n60\t- Lifecycle management: per-namespace scoping for multi-tenant isolation, and cleanup when the\n61\t  owning playground is deleted.\n62\t- Portability: the consuming configuration must be able to switch to the shared platform-provided\n63\t  PostgreSQL connection string (RHOAI 3.6) without rework.\n64\t\n65\t## Acceptance Criteria\n66\t\n67\t- A RAG-enabled playground in a namespace gets a per-namespace pgvector-capable PostgreSQL\n68\t  instance with no manual user provisioning or configuration of external infrastructure.\n69\t- The provisioned database runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance (not an\n70\t  inline provider).\n71\t- No custom container image is built: the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image (pgvector included)\n72\t  is used, referenced via the platform related-image variable so disconnected installs work.\n73\t- Resource requests/limits follow the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL values as the starting\n74\t  point, with any adjustment from the sprint-1 benchmark documented.\n75\t- Deleting the owning playground cleans up the provisioned PostgreSQL resources.\n76\t- The connection is exposed to the playground configuration as a reference that can later be\n77\t  swapped for the shared platform database connection string without rework.\n78\t\n79\t## HLR Traceability\n80\t\n81\t- AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box): provisioning half of the requirement.\n82\t- AC-4 (runs as a separate process, not inline).\n83\t- AC-5 (scoped for multi-tenant environments, per-namespace isolation).\n84\t- AC-6 (lightweight enough for resource-constrained environments): resource sizing scope.\n85\t\n86\t## Risks / Notes\n87\t\n88\t- This branch exists only if the go/no-go gate selects the operator path; if the operator layer\n89\t  does not land in time, the BFF-managed provisioning path (or bring-your-own PostgreSQL) delivers\n90\t  the default vector store instead.\n91\t- The operator layer's actual API surface is not known until RHAISTRAT-7164 delivers; the\n92\t  reconciliation design adapts to that surface.\n93\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac7f19a9efafe13c","agent_id":"a7ed42b29d881bc12","session_id":"eb96f7e6-35e1-46c5-82db-a48f5def6ca9","uuid":"0c0a8125-b9ec-4bc0-8399-6200db0a1f11","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:29:59.128Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-92a742eee52cd0e2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
