{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-baf4c7e229e71dda","type":"tool_result","content":"**Detailed**: ogx-distribution packages the OGX framework as a containerized Python service for RHOAI. It acts as a unified AI agent gateway that routes inference requests to configurable remote providers (vLLM, AWS Bedrock, IBM WatsonX, Azure, Vertex AI, OpenAI, Gemini, Anthropic), provides vector I/O through Milvus, PGVector, or Qdrant backends, and offers tool runtime capabilities including web search and file operations. The distribution uses PostgreSQL for both key-value and SQL-backed persistence of agent state, conversations, batches, and metadata. Authentication is handled via OAuth2 token validation with JWKS when configured. The container image is built on an AIPCC base image with Python dependencies installed from the RHEL AI Python Package Index via Hermeto-prefetched packages, and ships pre-fetched Docling and embedding model artifacts. [source: distribution/config.yaml:1-280, Dockerfile.konflux:1-58, distribution/entrypoint.sh:1-79]\n\n## Architectural Analysis\n--\n| 2 | OGX Server | Vector DB (Milvus / PGVector / Qdrant) | Configurable | HTTP/gRPC/SQL | Configurable (mTLS for Milvus) | Token / API key / password |\n| 3 | OGX Server | Inference Provider | Configurable | HTTP/HTTPS | TLS | API token |\n| 4 | OGX Server | PostgreSQL | 5432/TCP | PostgreSQL | Platform-delegated | Username/password |\n--\n| PGVector | SQL client | Optional | 5432/TCP | PostgreSQL | Configurable | Vector database via PostgreSQL extension |\n| Qdrant | HTTP/gRPC client | Optional | 6333/TCP (HTTP), 6334/TCP (gRPC) | HTTP or gRPC | HTTPS configurable | Vector database for RAG |\n| Brave Search | HTTP client | Optional | 443/TCP | HTTPS | TLS | Web search tool runtime |\n===\n**Detailed**: ogx-distribution packages the OGX framework as a containerized Python service for RHOAI. It acts as a unified AI agent gateway that routes inference requests to configurable remote providers (vLLM, AWS Bedrock, IBM WatsonX, Azure, Vertex AI, OpenAI, Gemini, Anthropic), provides vector I/O through Milvus, PGVector, or Qdrant backends, and offers tool runtime capabilities including web search and file operations. The distribution uses PostgreSQL for both key-value and SQL-backed persistence of agent state, conversations, batches, and metadata. Authentication is handled via OAuth2 token validation with JWKS when configured. The container image is built on an AIPCC base image with Python dependencies installed from the RHEL AI Python Package Index via Hermeto-prefetched packages, and ships pre-fetched Docling and embedding model artifacts. [source: distribution/config.yaml:1-280, Dockerfile.konflux:1-58, distribution/entrypoint.sh:1-79]\nOGX distribution follows a provider-plugin architecture where each API capability (inference, vector I/O, tool runtime, files, batches, responses, messages) is backed by one or more configurable providers. Providers are conditionally activated via environment variable guards (e.g., `${env.VLLM_URL:+vllm-inference}`), meaning the running configuration adapts to the deployment context without code changes. The distribution strips several inline providers (docling, faiss, milvus-inline, sentence-transformers) from the upstream build configuration, shipping only remote-capable providers suitable for production multi-worker deployments. [source: distribution/config.yaml:4-12, build/build.yaml:1-5]\n| **Certificate handling** | System trust store (inherited from UBI base); configurable CA paths for Milvus (`ca_pem_path`, `client_pem_path`) and auth (`tls_cafile`) | distribution/config.yaml:89-91,268 |\n| 2 | OGX Server | Vector DB (Milvus / PGVector / Qdrant) | Configurable | HTTP/gRPC/SQL | Configurable (mTLS for Milvus) | Token / API key / password |\n| Milvus | HTTP client | Optional | Configurable | HTTP/HTTPS | mTLS configurable | Remote vector database for RAG |","is_error":false}]},"parent_to