nk (configuration, benchmark, one provisioning path each). No scope\n64\tduplication: E002 (consume connection / configure provider) and the branch epics (provision the\n65\tdatabase) are complementary halves split along the gate line, the planning-relevant seam — not\n66\ttwo epics building the same surface. No work-product type mixing (E003's report is the natural\n67\tdeliverable of benchmark implementation work, not content authoring).\n68\t\n69\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n70\tE001 is a genuine Investigation: its outcome determines which branch epic exists, exactly the\n71\tgate the Staff Engineer Input directs the team to define. Both branch epics have `gated_by:\n72\tRHAISTRAT-8004-E001` present in their direct `dependencies` lists, and `gate_failure_impact`\n73\twith both `action` (remove / rewrite) and a concrete `fallback_approach` populated — real gates,\n74\tnot scheduling dependencies. All Implementation epics produce concrete artifacts (BFF\n75\tconfiguration code, benchmark harness + report, provisioning logic). No epic lists an\n76\tInvestigation dependency without `gated_by`.\n77\t\n78\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n79\tType-appropriate signal sets throughout: E001 carries `investigation_signals` (5-signal\n80\trubric); all four Implementation epics carry `ai_signals` (9-signal rubric) with matching\n81\tai-signals files. Signal values cross-checked against strategy content and `.context`:\n82\tE001's `source_accessibility: 0` / `human_judgment_required: -2` correctly reflect that the\n83\tgating answer is a pending human sprint-planning decision, not a readable record;\n84\t`architecture_claims: 1` rationales on E002/E003/branches cite architecture-context files that\n85\texist and do corroborate the claims (ogx-distribution.md documents PGVector as an optional\n86\tvector-io backend and the stripping of milvus-inline/faiss in the production build;\n87\tmodel-registry-operator.md documents the per-registry postgres Deployment pattern